Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||12-12-2001||12:30 PM||||Skitime's is built from the lower section of another GT front bumper. Lawrence is the other person who produced one of these.  They were slightly different (Skitime's has smaller lights & openings) but produced the same general appearance.  This type of part is superior to most aftermarket air dams because it is made from the Urethane-type bumper material, as opposed to rigid fiberglass.  It'll flex if hit, as opposed to just cracking and/or breaking.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||skitime||12-12-2001||02:19 PM||||Thanks for the compliments. Lawrence was the first to do the chin spoiler made from a GT nose.  I talked with him before making mine. Lawrence might of sold his car or at least was trying to sell it.  <P>Here is my car and chin spoiler <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080039-2.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P000821-1.jpg">    <P>And here is Lawrences' car and chin spoiler.   <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cool_Spoiler_Side.JPG">     <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cool_Spoiler_Front.JPG">    <BR><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
